CHAPTER.VERS:
And Saul said, Blessed be you

          {+}
         of Yahweh; for you

          {+}
         have had compassion on me.

Go, I pray you

          {+}
        , make yet more sure, and know and see his place where [the trace of] his foot is, [and] who has seen him there; for it is told me that he deals very subtly.

See therefore, and take knowledge of all the lurking-places where he hides himself, and come

          {+}
         again to me of a certainty, and I will go with you

          {+}
        : and it will come to pass, if he is in the land, that I will search him out among all the thousands of Judah.
